        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Mottled rash / livedo pattern"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mottled purplish net-like discolouration on both shins and dorsum of feet, right greater than left, for approximately 10–14 days; appearance considered more consistent with ischaemic/vascular change than dermatitis. Patient wondered whether it might relate to new washing powder or bore water; timing unclear."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right great and second toe symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Toes, especially the right great and second toes, feel cold and tingly at night and are somewhat sore after being on them a lot."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
